    "rules": "Classic Sudoku: Every row, column and 3x3 box must contain every number from 1 to 9.\nGerman Whispers: Every two consecutive digits along a green line must have a difference of at least 5.\nKropki Dots: Digits separated by a white dot are consecutive; digits separated by a black dot have a 1:2 ratio; if two digits are separated by a black&white dot, one must be multiple of the other.\nA dot placed at the corner intersection of four cells indicates that its condition applies to both diagonal pairs (top-left/bottom-right and top-right/bottom-left).",
